# The fourteen

Every block that was `planned` in spec/blocks.toml until 0.25.0, with the
corpus's own grammar and text that must escape identically on both paths:
`<angle>` & "quotes" in a label, a **bold** verdict, a link inside a turn.

::related
- [Architecture Plan](plans/product/2026-02-10-notesurf-plan.md) — produces
- research/ards-v3/manuscript/v1/ards-v3-paper.md — specific standard (cited as evidence for P2, P3)
- consumes: research/surfdoc/analysis/study-9.3/results/FINDINGS.md
- plans/ideas/2026-02-22-surfdoc-wiki-idea.md
- [Evil](javascript:alert(1)) — never
::

::turn[participant=brady time=2026-02-10T04:00Z role=human]
We're about to open-source ARDS v3. Should I file the provisionals first?
The filing fees are ~$1K each & Meng hasn't sent terms yet.
::

::turn[participant=claude time=2026-02-10T04:01Z role=ai model=opus]
Yes — file before launch. Two reasons:

1. **Prior art.** The moment ARDS v3 is public, anyone can cite it.
2. **12-month clock.** See [the plan](plans/plan.md).
::

